{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Like Reuben and Shimon they shall be to me.</b> Here Jacob gave the birthright to Joseph; and what is written (I Chronicles 5:1) ״ובחללו יצועי אביו נתנה בכורתו ליוסף״ — it is said so from this verse." "<b>And behold.</b> The opinion of Rashi, of blessed memory, is that the birthright of Joseph was not for the matter of inheritance but only for the matter of honor, that his sons would be called tribes." "<b>And the Ramban,</b> of blessed memory, rejects this, for it is impossible in any way that Joseph should be like the rest of the tribes in inheritance and the birthright be merely to be called two tribes; rather, the birthright of Joseph was for the matter of inheritance, and this is what the verse says ״בנחלתם״. And this is what Onkelos translated: ״תרין שבטין יפקון מבנוהי יקבלון חולקא ואחסנתא״ — two tribes shall issue from his sons, they shall receive a portion and an inheritance; for חולקא is the portion of the birthright, and אחסנתא is ordinary inheritance."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:06.011506880Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}